  "story": {
   "title": "门边的那把伞",
   "en": "Mara kept a yellow umbrella beside the front door. She had never liked the rain. To her, a rainy day meant wet shoes, a gray sky, and nowhere at all to go.\n\nBut one Saturday morning, the rain began to fall just as she opened her favorite book. She had planned to read all afternoon, and now the whole day felt ruined. Rain tapped softly on the roof, and the sound was almost like music. Her small gray cat, Pickle, jumped onto the chair beside her and purred, as if he understood exactly how she felt.\n\nMara made a cup of hot tea and cut herself a thick slice of apple cake. She sat at the kitchen table and watched the water run down the glass. Then she noticed something she had never noticed before. A little bird was sitting in the tree outside, washing itself in the rain and quite happy about it.\n\nAn hour later, the rain stopped. The sun came out, and the wet street turned gold. She took a deep breath and felt glad to be out again. Mara picked up her umbrella and stepped into the street. The air smelled clean and sweet. Pickle followed her to the door and blinked at the bright light.\n\nShe walked to the small shop on the corner and bought a fresh loaf of bread and a jar of strawberry jam. On the way home, she met her neighbor's old dog, who wagged his tail and followed her part of the way.\n\nThat evening, Mara sat by the window again, this time with a quiet smile. The umbrella by the door was still wet, but she no longer minded. Rain, she decided, was not the end of a day. It was only a soft, quiet beginning.",
   "zh": "玛拉在前门旁放着一把黄色的雨伞。她从来不喜欢下雨。对她来说，雨天意味着湿透的鞋子、灰蒙蒙的天空，还有哪儿也去不了的烦闷。\n\n可是有一个周六的早晨，她刚翻开最爱的书，雨就下了起来。她本打算读一整个下午，现在整天都好像被毁了。雨点轻轻敲着屋顶，那声音几乎像音乐一样。她的小灰猫皮克尔跳上旁边的椅子，发出呼噜呼噜的声音，好像完全懂她的心情。\n\n玛拉泡了一杯热茶，给自己切了厚厚一片苹果蛋糕。她坐在厨房的桌子旁，看着雨水顺着玻璃滑落。这时她注意到了一件从未留意过的事。窗外树上站着一只小鸟，正在雨里梳理羽毛，显得那么快活。\n\n一个小时后，雨停了。太阳出来了，湿漉漉的街道被染成金色。她深深吸了一口气，很高兴又走出了家门。玛拉拿起雨伞走到街上，空气闻起来干净又清甜。皮克尔跟着她来到门口，对着明亮的光眨了眨眼。\n\n她走到街角的小店，买了一条新鲜面包和一罐草莓酱。回家的路上，她遇见邻居家的老狗，它摇着尾巴，陪她走了一小段路。\n\n那天傍晚，玛拉又坐到窗边，这次脸上带着安静的笑。门边的伞还是湿的，可她已经不在意了。她想，雨并不是一天的结束，而只是一个温柔、安静的开始。"
  }
